# Commit, push, VPS sync (`sport-lead.ru`)

Commit and push stay **owner-gated**. VPS sync after a `main` push is **not** optional.

## Permissions (unchanged)

- Do not commit, tag, or `git push` unless the owner explicitly asked.
- Do not invent a commit when they only asked to change code.
- No `Co-authored-by` Cursor/agent trailers.

## After a successful `git push origin main`

The VPS clone is `/home/deploy/sport-leads` (`https://sport-lead.ru`). Sync path is Git only — no rsync/scp of the tree.

1. Push to `main` **must** start `.github/workflows/deploy-production.yml` (`on: push` + remaining `workflow_dispatch`).
2. If the push workflow did not appear: `gh workflow run "Deploy production" --ref main -f ref=main`.
3. Wait until the run succeeds (or report the failing job URL). Do not tell the owner "pushed" while VPS is still on the previous SHA.
4. Confirm health: `https://sport-lead.ru/healthz` (and `/health/ready` when the job did not already).

## Do not

- Push a non-`main` branch and expect production to follow.
- Skip deploy because "docs-only" or "the owner can dispatch later".
- `git reset --hard` / `git clean -fd` on the VPS by hand; the workflow already resets to the pushed SHA.

Media (`storage/`) is a separate SoT — dump/push does not copy files. DB stays VPS Postgres; agent tests stay on local Docker Postgres.
